--- CURRENT PROBLEM:
In performStoreDealsRefresh (line 3300-3364), deals from Steam and CheapShark are concatenated
without deduplication:
    const deals = [...steamDeals, ...cheapSharkDeals].sort(...)

This causes the same game to appear multiple times if:
- The same game is listed on both Steam and CheapShark
- The same game is listed multiple times in CheapShark with the same gameID but somehow not caught by prior dedup
- The same game is listed from the same reseller at different prices

SOLUTION:
Add a comprehensive deduplication step after combining deals, using the same logic that
already exists for CheapShark deals (group by gameID, then steamAppId, then normalized name;
keep the cheapest per group).

KEY FUNCTION: storeSeenKey (line 3269-3273)
- Returns unique key for each game
- Uses gameID if available
- Falls back to steamAppId
- Falls back to normalized game name

We need to apply this logic to deduplicate the combined deals array.
